   "heading": "How it works",
   "paragraphs": [
    "The tape alternates between two encodings. At the left turn it is blocks of ones and blocks of zeros, <code>0 1^13 0^5 1^4 0^5 1^4 0^5 1^4 0^2 1^12 0^4 &hellip;</code>; at the right turn it is blocks of ones whose lengths are mostly 3k+2 (2, 5, 8, 11, &hellip;) separated by single 0s. The rewriting is done by a zigzagging head, not one clean sweep, so turns at the ends are rare.",
    "The left end grows in bursts. From the second burst on, every burst adds a multiple of 1,065 cells, and after each one the first hundreds of cells of the tape are exactly as before: a burst rebuilds the left structure further out. How it does so, and why 1,065, is the open part."
